# Real, relaxed GaAs, 2 atoms/cell (1 Ga + 1 As), zincblende, primitive
# rhombohedral setting -- fetched from the Crystallography Open Database via
# stb-fetch (--unitcell primitive) and relaxed with SIESTA. This is the exact
# structure used in this workflow's real, physically-verified investigation
# (README section 4): the uncorrected cohesive energy comes out badly
# over-bound (BSSE's textbook signature), the BSSE correction fixes most of
# it, and a real vacuum/box-size bug -- found and fixed while investigating
# why the correction wasn't converging with --bsse-cutoff -- lives entirely
# in this same real dataset's story.
#
# Note the near-zero-but-not-exactly-zero terms below (e.g. 0.00395996 where
# an ideal zincblende cell would have exactly 0): this is a real relaxed
# structure, not a hand-typed ideal one -- small numerical asymmetry like
# this is normal and is explained in section 4 (it's also why stb-cohesive's
# own symmetry detector reports the trigonal subgroup R3m instead of the
# ideal cubic F-43m here, with zero practical effect on this calculation
# since each species has only 1 atom in the cell either way).

NumberOfSpecies    2
NumberofAtoms      2

%block ChemicalSpeciesLabel
 1   31   Ga
 2   33   As
%endblock ChemicalSpeciesLabel

LatticeConstant 1.0 Ang

AtomicCoordinatesFormat  Fractional

%block LatticeVectors
 0.00395996   2.86331622   2.86331617
 2.86331622   0.00395996   2.86331617
 2.86331622   2.86331622   0.00395996
%endblock LatticeVectors

%block AtomicCoordinatesAndAtomicSpecies
  0.00014953   0.00014953   0.00014953   1
  0.24984602   0.24984602   0.24984602   2
%endblock AtomicCoordinatesAndAtomicSpecies
